## DESCRIPTION
## Solve a maximimum linear optimization problem that is not in standard form.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('lines')
## Tagged by jjh2b

## DBsubject('WeBWorK')
## DBchapter('Linears and Linear Function')
## DBsection('Problem')
## Date('September 5, 2023')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'scaffold.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Matrix');

$Am = [ map { [ map { non_zero_random(-9, 9) } (1 .. 3) ] } (1 .. 4) ];
$A  = Matrix($Am);

$b    = ColumnVector(map { non_zero_random(-40, 40) } (1 .. 4));
$cm   = [ map { random(10, 40) } (1 .. 3) ];
$c    = ColumnVector($cm);
@beta = num_sort(random_subset(4, 1 .. 7));

# This finds the difference (1..7) - @beta;
%beta = map  { $_ => 1 } @beta;
@pi   = grep { !$beta{$_} } (1 .. 7);

for my $i (0 .. 3) {
    for my $j (0 .. 3) {
        $Bm->[$i][$j] =
            $beta[$j] <= 3        ? $Am->[$i][ $beta[$j] - 1 ]
            : $i == $beta[$j] - 4 ? 1
            :                       0;
    }
    for my $j (0 .. $#pi) {
        $Pim->[$i][$j] =
            $pi[$j] <= 3 ? $Am->[$i][ $pi[$j] - 1 ] : $i == $pi[$j] - 4 ? 1 : 0;
    }
}
$B     = Matrix($Bm);
$dbeta = abs($B->det);
$Bp    = $dbeta * $B->inverse;

$cbm->[$_] = $beta[$_] <= 3 ? $cm->[ $beta[$_] - 1 ] : 0 for (0..3);
$cpm->[$_] = $pi[$_] <= 3 ? $cm->[ $pi[$_] - 1 ] : 0 for (0..2);

$cb = ColumnVector($cbm);
$cp = ColumnVector($cpm);

$Bpb  = $Bp * $b;
$Pi   = Matrix($Pim);
$BpPi = $Bp * $Pi;

$z    = $cb . Vector($Bpb);
$crow = Vector($cb * $BpPi) - $dbeta * $cp;

BEGIN_PGML
Let
[```A = [$A], \qquad \mathbf{b} = [$b], \qquad \mathbf{c} = [$c] ```]

and [`\beta =\{`] [@ join(", ",@beta) @] [`\}`].  Recall that [`\mathbf{B}`] and  [`\mathbf{\Pi}`] are the columns of [`\mathbf{A}`] or [`\mathbf{I}`] from [`\beta`] and [`\pi`] respectively.  Find the following:

END_PGML

Scaffold::Begin();
Section::Begin('Definitions of B, \(\Pi\) and c');

BEGIN_PGML

a) [`\mathbf{B}=`][_]*{$B}
b) [`\mathbf{\Pi} =`] [_]*{$Pi}
c) [`d_{\beta}=`] [_]{$dbeta}
d) [`\mathbf{c}_{\beta}= `] [_]*{$cb}
e) [`\mathbf{c}_{\pi}= `] [_]*{$cp}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
First, the matrices [`\mathbf{B}`] and  [`\mathbf{\Pi}`] are the columns of [`\mathbf{A}`] or [`\mathbf{I}`] from [`\beta`] and [`\pi`] respectively. Also redefine [`\mathbf{c}`] to concatenate the zero vector of length 4.

a) [``` \mathbf{B} = [$B] ```]
b) [``` \mathbf{\Pi} = [$Pi] ```]
c) [`d_{\beta}`] is the absolute value of the determinant of [`\mathbf{B}`] or [$dbeta].
d) [`\mathbf{c}_{\beta}`] is the elements of [`\mathbf{c}`] selected from [`\beta`] or 
[``` \mathbf{c}_{\beta} = [$cb] ```]
e) [`\mathbf{c}_{\pi}`] is the elements of [`\mathbf{c}`] selected from [`\pi`] or 
[``` \mathbf{c}_{\pi} = [$cp] ```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

Section::End();

Section::Begin('Calculations');
BEGIN_PGML
For the following, recall that [`d_{\beta} = |\text{det}(\textbf{B})|`] and  [`\mathbf{B}' = d_{\beta} \mathbf{B}^{-1}`] to ensure that if [`\mathbf{B}`] is integral, then [`\mathbf{B}'`] is integral. 

a) [`\mathbf{B}'=`] [_]*{$Bp}
b) [`\mathbf{B}'\mathbf{b}=`] [_]*{$Bpb}
c) [`\mathbf{B}'\mathbf{\Pi}=`] [_]*{$BpPi}
d) [`\mathbf{c}_{\beta}^{\intercal}\mathbf{B}^{-1}\mathbf{b}=`] [_]{$z}
e) [`\mathbf{c}_{\beta}^{\intercal}\mathbf{B}^{-1}\mathbf{\Pi} - d_{\beta} \mathbf{c}_{\pi}^{\intercal} = `] [_]*{$crow}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
First, note that 
[``` \mathbf{B}^{-1} = [$B->inverse] ```]

a) [```\mathbf{B}' = d_{\beta} \mathbf{B}^{-1} =  [$Bp]```]
b) [``` \mathbf{B}' \mathbf{b} = [$Bpb] ```]
c) [``` \mathbf{B}'\mathbf{\Pi}= [$BpPi] ```]
d) [```\mathbf{c}_{\beta}^{\intercal}\mathbf{B}^{-1}\mathbf{b}= [$z]```]
e) [```\mathbf{c}_{\beta}^{\intercal}\mathbf{B}^{-1}\mathbf{\Pi} - d_{\beta} \mathbf{c}_{\pi}^{\intercal} = [$crow] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

Section::End();
Scaffold::End();
ENDDOCUMENT();
